        </div>
        <p class="text-muted">
          A bipolar membrane (BPM) consists of a cation-exchange layer (CEL) and an anion-exchange layer (AEL) chemically joined by an ultra-thin hydrophilic catalytic junction containing nanostructured transition metal oxides (e.g. ZrO2 or Fe(OH)x). Under reverse electrical bias, water molecules entering the junction dissociate catalytically:
        </p>
